window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-0310706ee8617b64"]={"zh":"<blockquote>  <p>来源：OpenAI 官方文档。本页为非 OpenAI 官方中文译本，可能滞后或存在翻译误差；如有冲突，以所链接的英文官方原文为准。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"prompting\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">提示设计</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整的文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"prompts\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"prompting-overview\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">提示设计概览</h2> <p>提示设计就是告诉 ChatGPT 你想了解、制作或更改什么。提示词 可以是问题、指令或目标。你不需要使用技术语法，也不必遵循 刻板的公式。先用自己的话说明需求，查看回复，再通过后续 消息逐步塑造结果。</p> <p>简短的提示词通常就够了。对于规模更大或更重要的任务，请包含 真正关键的部分：</p> <ul> <li><strong>目标：</strong> ChatGPT 应该做什么？</li> <li><strong>上下文：</strong> 哪些信息或来源会有帮助？</li> <li><strong>输出：</strong> 你需要什么格式、长度或详细程度？</li> <li><strong>边界：</strong> 哪些内容必须保持不变？ChatGPT 应避免什么？采取操作前，哪些事情 应先与你确认？</li> </ul> <p>只使用能提供帮助的部分。你不必填写每一项，也不必遵循 指定格式。</p> <p><a id=\"describe-the-result-you-need\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">描述你需要的结果</h2> <p>从结果说起，而不是先列出详细的步骤。如果受众或 格式会影响 ChatGPT 应生成的内容，也请把这些细节写明。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Turn these meeting notes into a short update for the project team.\nPut the decisions and next steps first.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：把这些会议记录整理成一份给项目团队的简短更新，先写出各项决定和后续步骤。</p> </blockquote> <p>这段提示词说明了要创建什么，以及谁会阅读它。如果流程本身 很重要，请描述流程。否则，请给 ChatGPT 留出空间，让它自行搜索、比较 信息并调整方法。</p> <p><a id=\"context\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"add-useful-context\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">添加有用的上下文</h2> <p>提供那些可能改变结果的信息。只添加真正相关的来源， 并说明 ChatGPT 应从每项来源中获取什么。</p> <ul> <li>如果希望 ChatGPT 对文档、电子表格、演示文稿或 PDF 文件进行 总结、比较、转换或<a href=\"#/article/a-1186da4cb8c2d6e2\">创建文件以供审查</a>，请附加这些文件。</li> <li>如果任务依赖视觉上下文，请添加截图、图表或其他<a href=\"#/article/a-b64a9457088d1171\">图像输入</a>。 请指出重要的区域，不要只依赖图像本身。</li> <li>如果答案依赖最新信息，请让 ChatGPT 使用<a href=\"#/article/a-eb946260804133fb\">网页搜索</a>； 如果你需要核查结果，还应要求提供来源。</li> <li>如果相关聊天需要共享文件、来源或本地文件夹，请使用<a href=\"#/article/a-3353f8f8f4d90d76\">项目</a>。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"use-connected-sources\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_5\">使用已连接的来源</h3> <p>如果 ChatGPT 可以访问已连接的来源，请明确它应到哪里查找，以及 应找到什么。你不需要描述它应执行的每一次搜索。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use the latest project plan in Drive and relevant decisions and updates from\nthe project's Slack channel to prepare a status update.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：使用 Drive 中最新的项目计划，以及项目 Slack 频道里相关的决定和更新，准备一份状态更新。</p> </blockquote> <p>已连接来源需要相应的插件，而且能否使用可能取决于 你的方案和工作区设置。</p> <p><a id=\"use-plugins\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_6\">使用插件</h3> <p>插件为 ChatGPT 和 Codex 提供可复用的指令，以及与 Google Drive、 Gmail、Slack 和 GitHub 等工具的连接。这两款产品都从同一个通用目录中 获取公开插件。请说明你需要的结果，并让当前使用的界面从其可用工具中 进行选择。在 ChatGPT 中，可以在消息输入框中键入 <code>@</code> 来选择特定插件。</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\"><strong>了解插件</strong><br>在 ChatGPT 和 Codex 中查找、安装和使用插件。</a></p> <p><a id=\"personalize-chatgpt\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"chatgpt\">个性化 ChatGPT</h3> <p>如果某些偏好应应用于所有聊天，请把它们作为自定义指令写入 <strong>Settings &gt; Personalization</strong>。只与当前聊天有关的细节应保留在 提示词中。</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-1e04f0e469568257?anchor=personalization\"><strong>查看个性化设置</strong><br>设置默认个性、自定义指令和其他应用偏好。</a></p> <p><a id=\"set-boundaries-that-prevent-real-problems\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">设置能够防止实际问题的边界</h2> <p>边界是 ChatGPT 为避免制造额外工作或执行你无意要求的操作而需要遵循的 少量指令。如果改错某个细节会导致结果无法使用，或你希望在某件事 影响他人之前先行审查，请添加相应边界。</p> <ul> <li>已批准的日期和预算数字必须保持不变。</li> <li>只能使用所提供的来源。遇到缺失的信息时应明确指出，而不是猜测。</li> <li>建议必须控制在规定的预算范围内。</li> <li>将消息准备为草稿。不要发送。</li> </ul> <p>只关注最重要的一两个边界。你不需要控制 ChatGPT 执行的 每一个步骤。</p> <p><a id=\"make-the-result-ready-to-use\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">让结果可以直接使用</h2> <p>告诉 ChatGPT 你打算如何使用结果。这有助于它选择合适的 长度、详细程度和组织方式。</p> <ul> <li>将其整理成一页摘要，方便主管在会议前快速浏览。把 决策和后续步骤放在最前面。</li> <li>将这些笔记整理成一封跟进邮件，其中包含各项决策、负责人和截止 日期。</li> <li>创建一张清晰的计划支出与实际支出对照表，并突出显示所有 超过 10% 的差异。</li> </ul> <p>对于重要工作，请让 ChatGPT 做最后检查，例如确认每项 行动都有负责人和截止日期，或标明它无法核实的信息。之后， 在使用或分享结果前由你亲自审查。</p> <p><a id=\"improve-the-result-with-follow-up-messages\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">通过后续消息改进结果</h2> <p>你的第一条提示词不必完美。查看结果，然后明确提出 你希望进行的修改。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Make the opening more direct, keep the evidence, and move the recommendation\nabove the background section.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：让开头更直接，保留证据，并把建议移到背景介绍之前。</p> </blockquote> <p>你可以补充缺少的来源、纠正方向、要求提供另一个方案，或 更改详细程度，而不必从头开始。</p> <p><a id=\"steering-and-queuing\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_10\">引导与排队</h3> <p>Codex 已在工作时，你无需等待当前运行结束，就可以发送另一条消息：</p> <ul> <li><strong>Steer</strong> 会把消息添加到当前运行中。可以用它改变方向、补充 缺失的细节或分享新信息。</li> <li><strong>Queue</strong> 会保存消息，供下一次运行使用。如果后续要求应当 等到当前工作结束再处理，请使用它。</li> </ul> <p>在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中，可以在 <a href=\"#/article/a-1e04f0e469568257?anchor=general\"><strong>Settings &gt; General &gt; Follow-up behavior</strong></a> 下选择默认行为。 已排队的消息会显示在消息输入框上方，你可以编辑、重新排序、发送或 删除它们。该设置还会显示一个快捷键，让你可以仅对某条消息采用另一种行为， 而不必更改默认设置。</p> <p>在 Codex CLI 中，当 Codex 正在工作时按 <kbd>Enter</kbd>，即可引导当前 轮次；按 <kbd>Tab</kbd> 则会将消息排到下一轮。详情请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?sectionMissing=cli-interactive-shortcuts\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">交互式快捷键（官网章节，需联网）</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3\">本地页面（未识别该章节）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"put-the-pieces-together\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_11\">将各个部分组合起来</h2> <p>如果要利用已连接的来源编写项目更新，一段完整的提示词可能如下：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Prepare a one-page project status update for Monday's leadership meeting. Use\nthe latest project plan in Drive and relevant decisions and updates from the\nproject's Slack channel.\n\nLead with the decisions leadership needs to make and the next steps. Summarize\nprogress, risks, owners, and due dates. Keep approved dates and budget figures\nunchanged. Flag any conflicting or missing information, and don't send or\npublish anything.\n\nBefore you finish, check that every next step has an owner and due date.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：为周一的领导层会议准备一页项目状态更新。使用 Drive 中最新的项目计划，以及项目 Slack 频道中相关的决定和更新。</p> <p>先列出领导层需要作出的决定和后续步骤，再总结进展、风险、负责人和截止日期。已批准的日期和预算数字必须保持不变；标出彼此冲突或缺失的信息，不要发送或发布任何内容。</p> <p>完成前，请检查每一项后续步骤是否都有负责人和截止日期。</p> </blockquote> <p>这段提示词涵盖了<strong>目标</strong>、<strong>上下文</strong>、<strong>输出</strong>和<strong>边界</strong>，然后 要求进行最终检查，但没有逐项规定每一个步骤。</p> <p><a id=\"use-voice-dictation\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_12\">使用语音听写</h2> <p>在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中，选择输入框中的 <strong>Dictate（听写）</strong>，然后开始说话。ChatGPT 会把语音转写到输入框中，让你可以在发送提示词前先检查和编辑。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：消息输入框中的语音听写指示器和已转写的提示词</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"threads\"></a> <a id=\"chats\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"prompting-examples-for-chat\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"chat\">Chat 的提示词示例</h2> <p>使用 Chat 来提问、构思、起草内容和处理日常决策。先说明你想得到的 结果，再只添加那些会改变答案的细节。</p> <p><a id=\"understand-a-topic\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_13\">理解一个主题</h3> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Explain how compound interest works for someone who has never invested.\nUse one concrete example and define any financial terms you introduce.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：向从未投资过的人解释复利如何运作。请举一个具体例子，并解释你提到的金融术语。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"draft-and-refine-writing\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_14\">起草和完善文字</h3> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Draft a friendly email declining this invitation because I will be traveling.\nKeep it under 120 words and leave the door open for a future event.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：起草一封友好的邮件，婉拒这次邀请，因为我届时要出行。全文不超过 120 个英文单词，并为以后参加活动留有余地。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"compare-options\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_15\">比较方案</h3> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Compare these two phone plans for one person who travels internationally twice\na year. Show the important differences in a table, then recommend one and explain\nthe tradeoff.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：为每年进行两次国际旅行的一个人比较这两种手机套餐。用表格列出重要差异，然后推荐其中一种并解释取舍。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"make-a-practical-plan\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_16\">制定实用计划</h3> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Plan five weekday dinners that take less than 30 minutes. Avoid peanuts, reuse\ningredients across meals, and finish with one consolidated shopping list.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：安排五顿工作日晚餐，每顿用时少于 30 分钟。避免使用花生，在不同餐食中重复利用食材，并在最后列出一份合并后的购物清单。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"prompting-for-work\"></a> <a id=\"prompting-in-work-mode\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"prompting-for-chatgpt-work\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"chatgpt-work\">为 ChatGPT Work 编写提示词</h2> <p>使用 Chat 处理快速提问、简短改写、头脑风暴和轻量级 草稿。对于需要利用不同来源或工具、包含一系列步骤、执行更改， 或产出较大型交付成果的任务，请使用 ChatGPT Work。</p> <p>在 ChatGPT Work 中，请描述所需结果、提供源材料、明确 受众，并说明你将如何审查工作。让 ChatGPT 制定计划、 收集所需信息、创建文件，并在结束前检查这些文件。</p> <p><a id=\"use-work-efficiently\"></a> <a id=\"use-work-mode-efficiently\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"use-chatgpt-work-efficiently\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"chatgpt-work_1\">高效使用 ChatGPT Work</h3> <p>ChatGPT Work 适合处理耗时或周期性任务，也适合生成可以 重复使用的成品文件。即使某项任务使用了更多额度，只要它能节省 时间、提高质量或帮助你作出重要决策，仍可能是值得的。</p> <p>先从一个你能够审查的结果开始：</p> <ul> <li>只包含相关来源，并在适用时限制日期范围。</li> <li>定义受众、输出格式和期望长度。</li> <li>区分必做工作与可选的改进或润色。</li> <li>如果工作方法很重要，请要求制定计划。在 ChatGPT 发送、发布或更改 他人所依赖的信息之前，必须获得你的批准。</li> <li>如果任务开始执行你已不再需要的工作，请缩小任务范围或停止任务。</li> </ul> <p>审查第一个结果、完善指令，并在工作流有效时重复使用它。</p> <p><a id=\"turn-source-material-into-finished-files\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_17\">将源材料转化为成品文件</h3> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use the attached quarterly reports to create a leadership brief and a six-slide\npresentation.\n\nThe audience is the executive team. Lead with the three decisions they need to\nmake, distinguish reported facts from your analysis, cite each number to its\nsource file, and check that the brief and slides agree before you finish.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：使用所附的季度报告，制作一份供领导层阅读的简报和一份六页演示文稿。受众是高管团队。先列出他们需要作出的三项决定；区分报告中陈述的事实与分析；为每个数字注明来源文件；完成前检查简报和幻灯片是否一致。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"research-a-decision\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_18\">研究一项决策</h3> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Research three customer-support platforms for a 50-person company. Compare\npricing, security, integrations, and migration effort using current sources.\nDeliver a recommendation memo with links, assumptions, and the questions we\nshould answer before signing a contract.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：为一家有 50 名员工的公司，研究三种客户支持平台。使用最新来源比较价格、安全性、集成能力和迁移工作量。提交一份建议备忘录，附上链接、所作假设，以及签署合同前需要回答的问题。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"coordinate-a-launch\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_19\">协调发布工作</h3> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Create a launch plan for the attached product brief. Include the timeline,\nowners, dependencies, risks, announcement draft, customer FAQ, and a checklist\nfor launch day. Flag any missing decisions before producing the final files.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：根据所附的产品简介制定发布计划，其中包括时间安排、负责人、依赖关系、风险、公告草稿、客户常见问题解答，以及发布当天的检查清单。生成最终文件前，指出尚未作出的决定。</p> </blockquote> <p>对于周期性工作，请先在普通聊天中完善提示词。输出变得 可靠后，可以<a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68?anchor=schedule-a-task-inside-a-chat\">在该聊天中安排任务</a>。 如果每次定时运行都应发起新聊天，则应改为创建独立的定时任务。</p> <p><a id=\"use-editor-context\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"prompting-codex\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex\">为 Codex 编写提示词</h2> <p>如果希望 ChatGPT 处理代码、代码库或开发者工具，请使用 Codex。 一段实用的 Codex 提示词会说明你想要的行为，指出相关代码或 复现步骤，保留重要约束，并说明如何验证 更改。</p> <p><a id=\"goal-mode\"></a></p> <p>对于多步骤任务，如果希望 Codex 在编辑前先调查并提出方法， 请在应用的消息输入框中输入 <code>/plan</code>。如果<a href=\"#/article/a-916e12c5bba5b9cc\">Goal 模式</a> 可用，请在计划完成后使用 <code>/goal</code> 设置一个持续目标。有关当前命令列表， 请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-6c3aed9dab628df5\">应用斜杠命令</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"how-to-read-these-examples\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_20\">如何阅读这些示例</h3> <p>每个工作流都包括：</p> <ul> <li><strong>何时使用</strong>，以及哪一种 Codex 界面最合适（IDE、CLI 或云端）。</li> <li>带有用户提示词示例的<strong>步骤</strong>。</li> <li><strong>上下文说明</strong>：Codex 会自动看到什么，以及哪些内容应由你附加。</li> <li><strong>验证</strong>：如何检查输出。</li> </ul> <blockquote> <p><strong>注意：</strong> IDE 扩展会自动把你打开的文件包含在上下文中。在 CLI 中，请明确指出路径，或者使用 <code>/mention</code> 和 <code>@</code> 路径自动补全来附加文件。</p> </blockquote> <p>Codex 会在<a href=\"#/article/a-668fd22585595004\">沙箱</a>中运行本地命令， 从而限制文件和网络访问。如果任务需要跨越该边界， Codex 会先按照你的审批策略处理，然后再继续。</p> <p><a id=\"explain-a-codebase\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_21\">解释代码库</h3> <p>如果你正在熟悉新项目、接手一项服务，或尝试理解某个协议、数据模型或请求流程，请使用此工作流。</p> <p><a id=\"ide-extension-workflow-fastest-for-local-exploration\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"ide\">IDE 扩展工作流（本地探索最快）</h4> <ol> <li>打开最相关的文件。</li> <li>选择你关心的代码（可选，但建议这样做）。</li> <li>向 Codex 输入提示词：</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Explain how the request flows through the selected code.\n\n   Include:\n   - a short summary of the responsibilities of each module involved\n   - what data is validated and where\n   - one or two \"gotchas\" to watch for when changing this\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：解释请求如何流经所选代码，并包括：相关各模块职责的简短总结；哪些数据会在哪里得到验证；修改时需要留意的一两个容易踩坑之处。</p> </blockquote> <p>验证：</p> <ul> <li>要求提供你能够核查的图表或清单：</li> </ul> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Summarize the request flow as a numbered list of steps. Then list the files involved.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：按编号步骤总结请求的流转过程，然后列出涉及的文件。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"cli-workflow-good-when-you-want-a-transcript-shell-commands\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"cli-shell\">CLI 工作流（适合需要对话记录和 shell 命令的情况）</h4> <ol> <li>启动交互式会话：</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">   codex\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>附加文件（可选）并输入提示词：</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   I need to understand the protocol used by this service. Read @foo.ts @schema.ts and explain the schema and request/response flow. Focus on required vs optional fields and backward compatibility rules.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：我需要了解此服务使用的协议。请阅读 @foo.ts 和 @schema.ts，解释数据结构（schema）以及请求/响应的流转过程，重点说明必填字段与可选字段的区别，以及向后兼容规则。</p> </blockquote> <p>上下文说明：</p> <ul> <li>你可以在消息输入框中使用 <code>@</code> 从工作区插入文件路径，也可以使用 <code>/mention</code> 附加特定文件。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"fix-a-bug\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_22\">修复错误</h3> <p>如果某个失败行为可以在本地复现，请使用此工作流。</p> <p><a id=\"cli-workflow-tight-loop-with-reproduction-and-verification\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"cli\">CLI 工作流（紧密衔接复现与验证）</h4> <ol> <li>在仓库根目录启动 Codex：</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">   codex\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>向 Codex 提供复现步骤，以及你怀疑有问题的文件：</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Bug: Clicking \"Save\" on the settings screen sometimes shows \"Saved\" but doesn't persist the change.\n\n   Repro:\n   1) Start the app: npm run dev\n   2) Go to /settings\n   3) Toggle \"Enable alerts\"\n   4) Click Save\n   5) Refresh the page: the toggle resets\n\n   Constraints:\n   - Do not change the API shape.\n   - Keep the fix minimal and add a regression test if feasible.\n\n   Start by reproducing the bug locally, then propose a patch and run checks.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：问题：在设置页面点击“保存”后，有时会显示“已保存”，但更改并没有保存下来。</p> <p>复现步骤：1）运行应用 npm run dev；2）前往 /settings；3）切换“启用提醒”（Enable alerts）；4）点击“保存”（Save）；5）刷新页面，开关又恢复了原状。</p> <p>约束：不要更改 API 的结构；尽量只做最小修复，并在可行时增加回归测试。请先在本地复现问题，再提出补丁并运行检查。</p> </blockquote> <p>上下文说明：</p> <ul> <li>由你提供：复现步骤和约束条件（它们比高层描述更重要）。</li> <li>由 Codex 提供：命令输出、发现的调用位置，以及它触发的任何堆栈跟踪。</li> </ul> <p>验证：</p> <ul> <li>修复后，Codex 应重新执行复现步骤。</li> <li>如果你有标准的检查流程，请让它运行该流程：</li> </ul> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">After the fix, run lint + the smallest relevant test suite. Report the commands and results.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：修复后运行代码检查（lint）和最小但相关的测试套件，并报告所运行的命令及结果。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"ide-extension-workflow\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"ide_1\">IDE 扩展工作流</h4> <ol> <li>打开你认为存在错误的文件，以及离它最近的调用方。</li> <li>向 Codex 输入提示词：</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Find the bug causing \"Saved\" to show without persisting changes. After proposing the fix, tell me how to verify it in the UI.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：找出导致界面显示“已保存”但实际没有保存更改的问题。提出修复方案后，告诉我如何在界面中验证修复是否有效。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"write-a-test\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_23\">编写测试</h3> <p>如果你希望明确界定要测试的确切范围，请使用此工作流。</p> <p><a id=\"ide-extension-workflow-selection-based\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"ide_2\">IDE 扩展工作流（基于选区）</h4> <ol> <li>打开包含该函数的文件。</li> <li>选中定义该函数的代码行。从命令面板中选择 \"Add to Codex Thread\"，将这些行添加到上下文中。</li> <li>向 Codex 输入提示词：</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Write a unit test for this function. Follow conventions used in other tests.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：为这个函数编写单元测试，并遵循其他测试所采用的约定。</p> </blockquote> <p>上下文说明：</p> <ul> <li>由 \"Add to Codex Thread\" 命令提供：所选代码行（这就是“行号”范围），以及打开的文件。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"cli-workflow-path-line-range-described-in-prompt\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"cli_1\">CLI 工作流（在提示词中描述路径和行号范围）</h4> <ol> <li>启动 Codex：</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">   codex\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>提示时给出函数名称：</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Add a test for the invert_list function in @transform.ts. Cover the happy path plus edge cases.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：为 @transform.ts 中的 invert_list 函数添加测试，覆盖正常情况以及边界情况。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"prototype-from-a-screenshot\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_24\">根据截图制作原型</h3> <p>如果希望把设计稿、截图或 UI 参考转化为可运行的原型，请使用此工作流。</p> <p><a id=\"cli-workflow-image-prompt\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"cli_2\">CLI 工作流（图像和提示词）</h4> <ol> <li>将截图保存到本地（例如 <code>./specs/ui.png</code>）。</li> <li>运行 Codex：</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">   codex\n</code></pre> <ol> <li> <p>将图像文件拖入终端，以附加到提示词。</p> </li> <li> <p>继续提供约束条件和结构要求：</p> </li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Create a new dashboard based on this image.\n\n   Constraints:\n   - Use react, vite, and tailwind. Write the code in typescript.\n   - Match spacing, typography, and layout as closely as possible.\n\n   Outputs:\n   - A new route/page that renders the UI\n   - Any small components needed\n   - README.md with instructions to run it locally\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：根据这张图片创建一个新的仪表板。要求：使用 React、Vite 和 Tailwind，以 TypeScript 编写代码；尽可能贴近图片中的间距、字体排版和布局。交付内容：一个能显示此界面的新路由/页面、所需的小型组件，以及一份说明如何在本地运行的 README.md。</p> </blockquote> <p>上下文说明：</p> <ul> <li>图像提供视觉要求，但实现约束（框架、路由、组件风格）仍需由你指定。</li> <li>请用文字说明图像没有展示的行为，例如悬停状态、验证规则或键盘交互。</li> </ul> <p>验证：</p> <ul> <li>让 Codex 运行开发服务器（如果允许），并准确告诉你应到哪里查看：</li> </ul> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Start the dev server and tell me the local URL/route to view the prototype.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：启动开发服务器，并告诉我查看这个原型所需的本地网址和路由。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"ide-extension-workflow-image-existing-files\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"ide_3\">IDE 扩展工作流（图像和现有文件）</h4> <ol> <li>在 Codex 聊天中附加图像（拖放或粘贴）。</li> <li>向 Codex 输入提示词：</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Create a new settings page. Use the attached screenshot as the target UI.\n   Follow design and visual patterns from other files in this project.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：创建一个新的设置页面，以附上的屏幕截图作为目标界面，并遵循此项目其他文件中的设计与视觉风格。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"iterate-on-ui-with-live-updates\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"ui\">通过实时更新迭代 UI</h3> <p>如果希望 Codex 编辑代码时形成紧密的“设计 → 微调 → 刷新 → 微调”循环，请使用此工作流。</p> <p><a id=\"cli-workflow-run-vite-then-iterate-with-small-prompts\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"cli-vite\">CLI 工作流（运行 Vite，然后通过简短提示词迭代）</h4> <ol> <li>启动 Codex：</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">   codex\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>在单独的终端窗口中启动开发服务器：</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">   npm run dev\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>让 Codex 进行更改：</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Propose 2-3 styling improvements for the landing page.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：为首页提出 2 到 3 项样式改进建议。</p> </blockquote> <ol> <li>选择一个方向，并通过简短、具体的提示词进行迭代：</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Go with option 2.\n\n   Change only the header:\n   - make the typography more editorial\n   - increase whitespace\n   - ensure it still looks good on mobile\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：采用方案 2。只修改页眉：让字体排版更有编辑设计感，增加留白，并确保在手机上仍然美观。</p> </blockquote> <ol> <li>继续提出聚焦的请求：</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Next iteration: reduce visual noise.\n   Keep the layout, but simplify colors and remove any redundant borders.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：下一轮请减少视觉杂乱。保留布局，但简化配色并移除多余边框。</p> </blockquote> <p>验证：</p> <ul> <li>Codex 更新代码时，请在浏览器中查看更改。</li> <li>提交你喜欢的更改，并还原你不喜欢的更改。</li> <li>如果你还原或修改了某项编辑，请告诉 Codex，以免它在处理下一条提示词时覆盖你的编辑。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"delegate-refactor-to-the-cloud\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_25\">将重构工作委派到云端</h3> <p>如果你想利用本地上下文设计方法，然后把耗时较长的实现工作委派给可以并行运行的云端聊天，请使用此工作流。</p> <p><a id=\"local-planning-ide\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"ide_4\">本地规划（IDE）</h4> <ol> <li>确保当前工作已经提交，或至少已用 Git stash 储藏，以便清楚地比较更改。</li> <li>让 Codex 制定重构计划。如果你可以使用 <code>$plan</code> 技能，请明确调用它：</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   $plan\n\n   We need to refactor the auth subsystem to:\n   - split responsibilities (token parsing vs session loading vs permissions)\n   - reduce circular imports\n   - improve testability\n\n   Constraints:\n   - No user-visible behavior changes\n   - Keep public APIs stable\n   - Include a step-by-step migration plan\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：$plan 用于先制定计划。我们需要重构身份验证子系统：拆分令牌解析、会话加载和权限处理的职责；减少循环导入；提升可测试性。约束：不改变用户可见行为；保持公开 API 稳定；提供逐步迁移计划。</p> </blockquote> <ol> <li>审查计划并协商修改：</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Revise the plan to:\n   - specify exactly which files move in each milestone\n   - include a rollback strategy\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：修改计划，明确每个里程碑中具体要移动哪些文件，并加入回滚策略。</p> </blockquote> <p>上下文说明：</p> <ul> <li>如果 Codex 可以在本地扫描当前代码（入口点、模块边界、依赖关系图线索），规划效果会更好。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"cloud-delegation-ide-cloud\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"ide-cloud\">云端委派（IDE → Cloud）</h4> <ol> <li>如果尚未设置，请先设置 <a href=\"#/article/a-73011d6801bc30d3\">Codex 云端环境</a>。</li> <li>点击提示词输入框下方的云朵图标，然后选择你的云端环境。</li> <li>输入下一条提示词时，Codex 会在云端创建一个新聊天，并继承现有聊天上下文（包括计划和所有本地源代码更改）。</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Implement Milestone 1 from the plan.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：按照计划实施第 1 个里程碑。</p> </blockquote> <ol> <li> <p>审查云端差异，必要时继续迭代。</p> </li> <li> <p>直接从云端创建 PR，或将更改拉取到本地进行测试和收尾。</p> </li> <li> <p>继续迭代计划中的其他里程碑。</p> </li> </ol> <p>委派到云端的任务会在隔离环境中运行。除非你为该环境启用互联网访问， 否则智能体阶段的互联网访问会保持关闭。进一步了解 <a href=\"#/article/a-b99b352f5f4ffa98\">云端互联网访问</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"do-a-local-code-review\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_26\">执行本地代码审查</h3> <p>如果希望在提交或创建 PR 前请另一位审查者检查，请使用此工作流。</p> <p><a id=\"cli-workflow-review-your-working-tree\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"cli_3\">CLI 工作流（审查你的工作树）</h4> <ol> <li>启动 Codex：</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">   codex\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>运行审查命令：</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   /review\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>命令用途：启动 Codex 代码审查；命令本身需原样输入。</p> </blockquote> <ol> <li>可选：提供自定义的关注重点指令：</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   /review Focus on edge cases and security issues\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：运行 /review，重点检查边界情况和安全问题。</p> </blockquote> <p>验证：</p> <ul> <li>根据审查反馈应用修复，然后再次运行 <code>/review</code>，确认问题已经解决。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"review-a-github-pull-request\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"github-pull-request\">审查 GitHub pull request</h3> <p>如果希望在不把分支拉取到本地的情况下获得审查反馈，请使用此工作流。</p> <p>在使用此功能前，请在你的仓库上启用 Codex <strong>Code review</strong>。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-ba7354e174823641\">代码审查</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"github-workflow-comment-driven\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"github\">GitHub 工作流（由评论驱动）</h4> <ol> <li>在 GitHub 上打开 pull request。</li> <li>留下一条评论，标记 Codex 并明确给出关注领域：</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   @codex review\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>操作含义：在 GitHub 拉取请求的评论中提及 @codex，并请求它进行审查。</p> </blockquote> <ol> <li>可选：提供更明确的指令。</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   @codex review for security vulnerabilities and security concerns\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：@codex，请进行审查，并重点查找安全漏洞与安全隐患。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"update-documentation\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_27\">更新文档</h3> <p>如果需要进行准确、清晰的文档更改，请使用此工作流。</p> <p><a id=\"ide-or-cli-workflow-local-edits-local-validation\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"ide-cli\">IDE 或 CLI 工作流（本地编辑和本地验证）</h4> <ol> <li>确定要更改的文档文件并将其打开（IDE），或用 <code>@</code> 提及这些文件（IDE 或 CLI）。</li> <li>向 Codex 提供范围和验证要求：</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Update the \"advanced features\" documentation to provide authentication troubleshooting guidance. Verify that all links are valid.\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>中文意思：更新“高级功能”文档，补充身份验证故障排查指南，并确认所有链接都有效。</p> </blockquote> <ol> <li>Codex 起草更改后，审查文档并按需迭代。</li> </ol> <p>验证：</p> <ul> <li>阅读渲染后的页面。</li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"prompting\">Prompting</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"prompts\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"prompting-overview\">Prompting overview</h2> <p>Prompting is how you tell ChatGPT what you want to know, make, or change. A prompt can be a question, an instruction, or a goal. You don't need technical syntax or a rigid formula. Start in your own words, review the response, and use follow-up messages to shape the result.</p> <p>A short prompt is often enough. For larger or more important tasks, include the parts that matter:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Goal:</strong> What should ChatGPT do?</li> <li><strong>Context:</strong> What information or sources will help?</li> <li><strong>Output:</strong> What format, length, or level of detail do you need?</li> <li><strong>Boundaries:</strong> What must stay unchanged? What should ChatGPT avoid or check with you before it acts?</li> </ul> <p>Use only the parts that help. You don't need to fill in every item or follow a required format.</p> <h2 id=\"describe-the-result-you-need\">Describe the result you need</h2> <p>Start with the result, not a detailed list of steps. Include the audience or format when those details change what ChatGPT should produce.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Turn these meeting notes into a short update for the project team.\nPut the decisions and next steps first.\n</code></pre> <p>This prompt explains what to create and who will read it. Describe a process when the process itself matters. Otherwise, leave ChatGPT room to search, compare information, and adjust its approach.</p> <p><a id=\"context\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"add-useful-context\">Add useful context</h2> <p>Share the information that could change the result. Add only the sources that matter, and explain what ChatGPT should take from each one.</p> <ul> <li>Attach documents, spreadsheets, presentations, or PDF files when you want ChatGPT to summarize, compare, transform, or <a href=\"#/article/a-1186da4cb8c2d6e2\">create files for review</a>.</li> <li>Add a screenshot, diagram, or other <a href=\"#/article/a-b64a9457088d1171\">image input</a> when the task depends on visual context. Point out the area that matters instead of relying on the image alone.</li> <li>Ask ChatGPT to use <a href=\"#/article/a-eb946260804133fb\">web search</a> when the answer depends on current information, and ask for sources when you need to check the result.</li> <li>Use a <a href=\"#/article/a-3353f8f8f4d90d76\">project</a> when related chats should share files, sources, or a local folder.</li> </ul> <h3 id=\"use-connected-sources\">Use connected sources</h3> <p>When ChatGPT has access to connected sources, name where it should look and what it should find. You don't need to describe every search it should run.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use the latest project plan in Drive and relevant decisions and updates from\nthe project's Slack channel to prepare a status update.\n</code></pre> <p>Connected sources require the matching plugin, and availability can depend on your plan and workspace settings.</p> <h3 id=\"use-plugins\">Use plugins</h3> <p>Plugins give ChatGPT and Codex reusable instructions and connections to tools such as Google Drive, Gmail, Slack, and GitHub. Both products draw public plugins from the same universal directory. Ask for the result you need and let the active surface choose from the tools available to it. In ChatGPT, type <code>@</code> in the composer to choose a specific plugin.</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\"><strong>Learn about plugins</strong><br>Find, install, and use plugins in ChatGPT and Codex.</a></p> <h3 id=\"personalize-chatgpt\">Personalize ChatGPT</h3> <p>Put preferences that should apply across chats in <strong>Settings &gt; Personalization</strong> as custom instructions. Keep details that matter only to the current chat in the prompt.</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-1e04f0e469568257?anchor=personalization\"><strong>Review personalization settings</strong><br>Set a default personality, custom instructions, and other app preferences.</a></p> <h2 id=\"set-boundaries-that-prevent-real-problems\">Set boundaries that prevent real problems</h2> <p>Boundaries are the few instructions ChatGPT needs to avoid creating extra work or taking an action you didn't intend. Add one when changing the wrong detail would make the result unusable, or when you want to review something before it affects other people.</p> <ul> <li>Keep the approved dates and budget figures unchanged.</li> <li>Use only the supplied sources. Flag missing information instead of guessing.</li> <li>Keep recommendations within the stated budget.</li> <li>Prepare the message as a draft. Don't send it.</li> </ul> <p>Focus on the one or two boundaries that matter most. You don't need to control every step ChatGPT takes.</p> <h2 id=\"make-the-result-ready-to-use\">Make the result ready to use</h2> <p>Tell ChatGPT how you plan to use the result. This helps it choose the right length, level of detail, and organization.</p> <ul> <li>Make this a one-page summary a director can scan before the meeting. Put the decision and next steps first.</li> <li>Turn these notes into a follow-up email with the decisions, owners, and due dates.</li> <li>Create a clear table of planned versus actual spending and highlight any difference over 10%.</li> </ul> <p>For important work, ask ChatGPT for a final check, such as confirming every action item has an owner and due date or flagging information it couldn't verify. Then review the result yourself before you use or share it.</p> <h2 id=\"improve-the-result-with-follow-up-messages\">Improve the result with follow-up messages</h2> <p>Your first prompt doesn't need to be perfect. Review the result, then ask for the specific change you want.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Make the opening more direct, keep the evidence, and move the recommendation\nabove the background section.\n</code></pre> <p>You can add a missing source, correct the direction, ask for another option, or change the level of detail without starting over.</p> <h3 id=\"steering-and-queuing\">Steering and queuing</h3> <p>When Codex is already working, you can send another message without waiting for the current run to finish:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Steer</strong> adds the message to the current run. Use it to change direction, add a missing detail, or share new information.</li> <li><strong>Queue</strong> saves the message for the next run. Use it for a follow-up that should wait until the current work finishes.</li> </ul> <p>In the ChatGPT desktop app, choose the default under <a href=\"#/article/a-1e04f0e469568257?anchor=general\"><strong>Settings &gt; General &gt; Follow-up behavior</strong></a>. Queued messages appear above the composer, where you can edit, reorder, send, or delete them. The setting also shows the shortcut for using the other behavior for one message without changing your default.</p> <p>In Codex CLI, press <kbd>Enter</kbd> while Codex is working to steer the current turn, or press <kbd>Tab</kbd> to queue the message for the next turn. See the <a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?sectionMissing=cli-interactive-shortcuts\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">interactive shortcuts (official section, online)</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3\">Local page (section not recognized)</a> for details.</p> <h2 id=\"put-the-pieces-together\">Put the pieces together</h2> <p>For a project update that uses connected sources, a complete prompt might look like this:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Prepare a one-page project status update for Monday's leadership meeting. Use\nthe latest project plan in Drive and relevant decisions and updates from the\nproject's Slack channel.\n\nLead with the decisions leadership needs to make and the next steps. Summarize\nprogress, risks, owners, and due dates. Keep approved dates and budget figures\nunchanged. Flag any conflicting or missing information, and don't send or\npublish anything.\n\nBefore you finish, check that every next step has an owner and due date.\n</code></pre> <p>This prompt covers the <strong>Goal</strong>, <strong>Context</strong>, <strong>Output</strong>, and <strong>Boundaries</strong>, then asks for a final check without spelling out every step.</p> <h2 id=\"use-voice-dictation\">Use voice dictation</h2> <p>In the ChatGPT desktop app, select <strong>Dictate</strong> in the composer, then start talking. ChatGPT transcribes your speech into the composer so you can review and edit it before sending the prompt.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Voice dictation indicator in the composer with a transcribed prompt</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"threads\"></a> <a id=\"chats\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"prompting-examples-for-chat\">Prompting examples for Chat</h2> <p>Use Chat for questions, ideas, drafts, and everyday decisions. Start with the outcome you want, then add detail only when it changes the answer.</p> <h3 id=\"understand-a-topic\">Understand a topic</h3> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Explain how compound interest works for someone who has never invested.\nUse one concrete example and define any financial terms you introduce.\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"draft-and-refine-writing\">Draft and refine writing</h3> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Draft a friendly email declining this invitation because I will be traveling.\nKeep it under 120 words and leave the door open for a future event.\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"compare-options\">Compare options</h3> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Compare these two phone plans for one person who travels internationally twice\na year. Show the important differences in a table, then recommend one and explain\nthe tradeoff.\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"make-a-practical-plan\">Make a practical plan</h3> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Plan five weekday dinners that take less than 30 minutes. Avoid peanuts, reuse\ningredients across meals, and finish with one consolidated shopping list.\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"prompting-for-work\"></a> <a id=\"prompting-in-work-mode\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"prompting-for-chatgpt-work\">Prompting for ChatGPT Work</h2> <p>Use Chat for quick questions, short rewrites, brainstorming, and lightweight drafts. Use ChatGPT Work for tasks that draw on different sources or tools, involve a sequence of steps, make changes, or produce a larger deliverable.</p> <p>In ChatGPT Work, describe the result you need, provide the source material, name the audience, and explain how you'll review the work. Ask ChatGPT to plan, gather the needed information, create files, and check them before it finishes.</p> <p><a id=\"use-work-efficiently\"></a> <a id=\"use-work-mode-efficiently\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"use-chatgpt-work-efficiently\">Use ChatGPT Work efficiently</h3> <p>ChatGPT Work is useful for time-consuming or recurring tasks, or for finished files you can reuse. A task that uses more credits can still be worthwhile if it saves time, improves quality, or helps you make an important decision.</p> <p>Start with one result you can review:</p> <ul> <li>Include only relevant sources and limit the date range when appropriate.</li> <li>Define the audience, output format, and desired length.</li> <li>Separate required work from optional improvements or polish.</li> <li>Ask for a plan when the approach matters. Require your approval before ChatGPT sends, publishes, or changes information other people rely on.</li> <li>Narrow or stop the task if it starts doing work you no longer need.</li> </ul> <p>Review the first result, refine the instructions, and reuse the workflow when it works.</p> <h3 id=\"turn-source-material-into-finished-files\">Turn source material into finished files</h3> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use the attached quarterly reports to create a leadership brief and a six-slide\npresentation.\n\nThe audience is the executive team. Lead with the three decisions they need to\nmake, distinguish reported facts from your analysis, cite each number to its\nsource file, and check that the brief and slides agree before you finish.\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"research-a-decision\">Research a decision</h3> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Research three customer-support platforms for a 50-person company. Compare\npricing, security, integrations, and migration effort using current sources.\nDeliver a recommendation memo with links, assumptions, and the questions we\nshould answer before signing a contract.\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"coordinate-a-launch\">Coordinate a launch</h3> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Create a launch plan for the attached product brief. Include the timeline,\nowners, dependencies, risks, announcement draft, customer FAQ, and a checklist\nfor launch day. Flag any missing decisions before producing the final files.\n</code></pre> <p>For recurring work, first refine the prompt in a normal chat. After the output is reliable, <a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68?anchor=schedule-a-task-inside-a-chat\">schedule a task inside that chat</a>. Create a standalone scheduled task instead when each scheduled run should start a new chat.</p> <p><a id=\"use-editor-context\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"prompting-codex\">Prompting Codex</h2> <p>Use Codex when you want ChatGPT to work with code, a codebase, or developer tools. A useful Codex prompt names the behavior you want, points to the relevant code or reproduction steps, preserves important constraints, and says how to verify the change.</p> <p><a id=\"goal-mode\"></a></p> <p>For a multi-step task, enter <code>/plan</code> in the app composer when you want Codex to investigate and propose an approach before editing. When <a href=\"#/article/a-916e12c5bba5b9cc\">Goal mode</a> is available, use <code>/goal</code> after the plan to set a persistent goal. See the <a href=\"#/article/a-6c3aed9dab628df5\">app slash commands</a> for the current command list.</p> <h3 id=\"how-to-read-these-examples\">How to read these examples</h3> <p>Each workflow includes:</p> <ul> <li><strong>When to use it</strong> and which Codex surface fits best (IDE, CLI, or cloud).</li> <li><strong>Steps</strong> with example user prompts.</li> <li><strong>Context notes</strong>: what Codex automatically sees vs what you should attach.</li> <li><strong>Verification</strong>: how to check the output.</li> </ul> <blockquote> <p><strong>Note:</strong> The IDE extension automatically includes your open files as context. In the CLI, mention paths explicitly, or attach files with <code>/mention</code> and <code>@</code> path autocomplete.</p> </blockquote> <p>Codex runs local commands inside a <a href=\"#/article/a-668fd22585595004\">sandbox</a> that limits file and network access. If a task needs to cross that boundary, Codex follows your approval policy before continuing.</p> <h3 id=\"explain-a-codebase\">Explain a codebase</h3> <p>Use this when you are onboarding, inheriting a service, or trying to reason about a protocol, data model, or request flow.</p> <h4 id=\"ide-extension-workflow-fastest-for-local-exploration\">IDE extension workflow (fastest for local exploration)</h4> <ol> <li>Open the most relevant files.</li> <li>Select the code you care about (optional but recommended).</li> <li>Prompt Codex:</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Explain how the request flows through the selected code.\n\n   Include:\n   - a short summary of the responsibilities of each module involved\n   - what data is validated and where\n   - one or two \"gotchas\" to watch for when changing this\n</code></pre> <p>Verification:</p> <ul> <li>Ask for a diagram or checklist you can verify:</li> </ul> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Summarize the request flow as a numbered list of steps. Then list the files involved.\n</code></pre> <h4 id=\"cli-workflow-good-when-you-want-a-transcript-shell-commands\">CLI workflow (good when you want a transcript + shell commands)</h4> <ol> <li>Start an interactive session:</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">   codex\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>Attach the files (optional) and prompt:</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   I need to understand the protocol used by this service. Read @foo.ts @schema.ts and explain the schema and request/response flow. Focus on required vs optional fields and backward compatibility rules.\n</code></pre> <p>Context notes:</p> <ul> <li>You can use <code>@</code> in the composer to insert file paths from the workspace, or <code>/mention</code> to attach a specific file.</li> </ul> <h3 id=\"fix-a-bug\">Fix a bug</h3> <p>Use this when you have a failing behavior you can reproduce locally.</p> <h4 id=\"cli-workflow-tight-loop-with-reproduction-and-verification\">CLI workflow (tight loop with reproduction and verification)</h4> <ol> <li>Start Codex at the repo root:</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">   codex\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>Give Codex a reproduction recipe, plus the file(s) you suspect:</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Bug: Clicking \"Save\" on the settings screen sometimes shows \"Saved\" but doesn't persist the change.\n\n   Repro:\n   1) Start the app: npm run dev\n   2) Go to /settings\n   3) Toggle \"Enable alerts\"\n   4) Click Save\n   5) Refresh the page: the toggle resets\n\n   Constraints:\n   - Do not change the API shape.\n   - Keep the fix minimal and add a regression test if feasible.\n\n   Start by reproducing the bug locally, then propose a patch and run checks.\n</code></pre> <p>Context notes:</p> <ul> <li>Supplied by you: the repro steps and constraints (these matter more than a high-level description).</li> <li>Supplied by Codex: command output, discovered call sites, and any stack traces it triggers.</li> </ul> <p>Verification:</p> <ul> <li>Codex should re-run the repro steps after the fix.</li> <li>If you have a standard check pipeline, ask it to run it:</li> </ul> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">After the fix, run lint + the smallest relevant test suite. Report the commands and results.\n</code></pre> <h4 id=\"ide-extension-workflow\">IDE extension workflow</h4> <ol> <li>Open the file where you think the bug lives, plus its nearest caller.</li> <li>Prompt Codex:</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Find the bug causing \"Saved\" to show without persisting changes. After proposing the fix, tell me how to verify it in the UI.\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"write-a-test\">Write a test</h3> <p>Use this when you want to define the exact scope to test.</p> <h4 id=\"ide-extension-workflow-selection-based\">IDE extension workflow (selection-based)</h4> <ol> <li>Open the file with the function.</li> <li>Select the lines that define the function. Choose \"Add to Codex Thread\" from command palette to add these lines to the context.</li> <li>Prompt Codex:</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Write a unit test for this function. Follow conventions used in other tests.\n</code></pre> <p>Context notes:</p> <ul> <li>Supplied by \"Add to Codex Thread\" command: the selected lines (this is the \"line number\" scope), plus open files.</li> </ul> <h4 id=\"cli-workflow-path-line-range-described-in-prompt\">CLI workflow (path + line range described in prompt)</h4> <ol> <li>Start Codex:</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">   codex\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>Prompt with a function name:</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Add a test for the invert_list function in @transform.ts. Cover the happy path plus edge cases.\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"prototype-from-a-screenshot\">Prototype from a screenshot</h3> <p>Use this when you want to turn a design mock, screenshot, or UI reference into a working prototype.</p> <h4 id=\"cli-workflow-image-prompt\">CLI workflow (image + prompt)</h4> <ol> <li>Save your screenshot locally (for example <code>./specs/ui.png</code>).</li> <li>Run Codex:</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">   codex\n</code></pre> <ol> <li> <p>Drag the image file into the terminal to attach it to the prompt.</p> </li> <li> <p>Follow up with constraints and structure:</p> </li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Create a new dashboard based on this image.\n\n   Constraints:\n   - Use react, vite, and tailwind. Write the code in typescript.\n   - Match spacing, typography, and layout as closely as possible.\n\n   Outputs:\n   - A new route/page that renders the UI\n   - Any small components needed\n   - README.md with instructions to run it locally\n</code></pre> <p>Context notes:</p> <ul> <li>The image provides visual requirements, but you still need to specify the implementation constraints (framework, routing, component style).</li> <li>Include behavior the image doesn't show in text, such as hover states, validation rules, or keyboard interactions.</li> </ul> <p>Verification:</p> <ul> <li>Ask Codex to run the dev server (if allowed) and tell you exactly where to look:</li> </ul> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Start the dev server and tell me the local URL/route to view the prototype.\n</code></pre> <h4 id=\"ide-extension-workflow-image-existing-files\">IDE extension workflow (image + existing files)</h4> <ol> <li>Attach the image in the Codex chat (drag-and-drop or paste).</li> <li>Prompt Codex:</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Create a new settings page. Use the attached screenshot as the target UI.\n   Follow design and visual patterns from other files in this project.\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"iterate-on-ui-with-live-updates\">Iterate on UI with live updates</h3> <p>Use this when you want a tight \"design → tweak → refresh → tweak\" loop while Codex edits code.</p> <h4 id=\"cli-workflow-run-vite-then-iterate-with-small-prompts\">CLI workflow (run Vite, then iterate with small prompts)</h4> <ol> <li>Start Codex:</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">   codex\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>Start the dev server in a separate terminal window:</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">   npm run dev\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>Prompt Codex to make changes:</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Propose 2-3 styling improvements for the landing page.\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>Pick a direction and iterate with small, specific prompts:</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Go with option 2.\n\n   Change only the header:\n   - make the typography more editorial\n   - increase whitespace\n   - ensure it still looks good on mobile\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>Repeat with focused requests:</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Next iteration: reduce visual noise.\n   Keep the layout, but simplify colors and remove any redundant borders.\n</code></pre> <p>Verification:</p> <ul> <li>Review changes in the browser as Codex updates the code.</li> <li>Commit changes that you like and revert those that you don't.</li> <li>If you revert or change an edit, tell Codex so it doesn't overwrite your edit when it works on the next prompt.</li> </ul> <h3 id=\"delegate-refactor-to-the-cloud\">Delegate refactor to the cloud</h3> <p>Use this when you want to design an approach with local context, then delegate the long implementation to a cloud chat that can run in parallel.</p> <h4 id=\"local-planning-ide\">Local planning (IDE)</h4> <ol> <li>Make sure your current work is committed or at least stashed so you can compare changes cleanly.</li> <li>Ask Codex to produce a refactor plan. If you have the <code>$plan</code> skill available, invoke it explicitly:</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   $plan\n\n   We need to refactor the auth subsystem to:\n   - split responsibilities (token parsing vs session loading vs permissions)\n   - reduce circular imports\n   - improve testability\n\n   Constraints:\n   - No user-visible behavior changes\n   - Keep public APIs stable\n   - Include a step-by-step migration plan\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>Review the plan and negotiate changes:</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Revise the plan to:\n   - specify exactly which files move in each milestone\n   - include a rollback strategy\n</code></pre> <p>Context notes:</p> <ul> <li>Planning works best when Codex can scan the current code locally (entrypoints, module boundaries, dependency graph hints).</li> </ul> <h4 id=\"cloud-delegation-ide-cloud\">Cloud delegation (IDE → Cloud)</h4> <ol> <li>If you haven't already done so, set up a <a href=\"#/article/a-73011d6801bc30d3\">Codex cloud environment</a>.</li> <li>Click on the cloud icon beneath the prompt composer and select your cloud environment.</li> <li>When you enter the next prompt, Codex creates a new chat in the cloud that carries over the existing chat context (including the plan and any local source changes).</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Implement Milestone 1 from the plan.\n</code></pre> <ol> <li> <p>Review the cloud diff, iterate if needed.</p> </li> <li> <p>Create a PR directly from the cloud or pull changes locally to test and finish up.</p> </li> <li> <p>Iterate on additional milestones of the plan.</p> </li> </ol> <p>Tasks delegated to the cloud run in isolated environments. Internet access is off during the agent phase unless you enable it for the environment. Learn more about <a href=\"#/article/a-b99b352f5f4ffa98\">cloud internet access</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"do-a-local-code-review\">Do a local code review</h3> <p>Use this when you want a second set of eyes before committing or creating a PR.</p> <h4 id=\"cli-workflow-review-your-working-tree\">CLI workflow (review your working tree)</h4> <ol> <li>Start Codex:</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">   codex\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>Run the review command:</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   /review\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>Optional: provide custom focus instructions:</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   /review Focus on edge cases and security issues\n</code></pre> <p>Verification:</p> <ul> <li>Apply fixes based on review feedback, then rerun <code>/review</code> to confirm you resolved the issues.</li> </ul> <h3 id=\"review-a-github-pull-request\">Review a GitHub pull request</h3> <p>Use this when you want review feedback without pulling the branch locally.</p> <p>Before you can use this, enable Codex <strong>Code review</strong> on your repository. See <a href=\"#/article/a-ba7354e174823641\">Code review</a>.</p> <h4 id=\"github-workflow-comment-driven\">GitHub workflow (comment-driven)</h4> <ol> <li>Open the pull request on GitHub.</li> <li>Leave a comment that tags Codex with explicit focus areas:</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   @codex review\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>Optional: Provide more explicit instructions.</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   @codex review for security vulnerabilities and security concerns\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"update-documentation\">Update documentation</h3> <p>Use this when you need an accurate, clear documentation change.</p> <h4 id=\"ide-or-cli-workflow-local-edits-local-validation\">IDE or CLI workflow (local edits + local validation)</h4> <ol> <li>Identify the doc file(s) to change and open them (IDE) or <code>@</code> mention them (IDE or CLI).</li> <li>Prompt Codex with scope and validation requirements:</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Update the \"advanced features\" documentation to provide authentication troubleshooting guidance. Verify that all links are valid.\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>After Codex drafts the changes, review the documentation and iterate as needed.</li> </ol> <p>Verification:</p> <ul> <li>Read the rendered page.</li> </ul>"};
